# Cross-platform line-ending hygiene: store text as LF in the repo, check out
# native. Keeps a Windows clone from rewriting every file to CRLF (and back).
* text=auto

# Explicit for the files we ship.
*.hpp   text
*.cpp   text
*.txt   text
*.md    text
*.json  text
*.yml   text
CMakeLists.txt text

# Fuzz seed corpora are RAW BYTES — sealed blobs and length-prefixed records.
# text=auto would leave their handling to a heuristic, and one seed
# (unseal/sealed_empty) contains a bare LF, so a Windows checkout could rewrite
# it to CRLF and silently corrupt the seed. Mark them binary explicitly.
tests/fuzz/corpus/** -text
tests/fuzz/corpus/README.md text
